WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:01.667
-Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.000
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.100
You guys, it's Veterans Day
and --

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.868
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.000
[ Whistling ]

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.834
Tonight, our audience is made up
of veterans and active military.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.467
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:17.400
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.701
Welcome.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.200
Between all of you out here

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.834
and Sylvester Stallone
backstage,

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.901
I've never felt so safe
in my entire life.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:27.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.767
I just want to say to everyone
here and watching at home,

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.434
thank you for protecting us
from our biggest threats,

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.767
both foreign

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.868
and domestic.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.400
You know --

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.334
[ Cheering ]

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.033
You know, I could never do what
all of you guys do.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.300
The closest I've been
to a war zone was this morning

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.534
when I logged on to Twitter.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:49.501
It was unbelievable.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.167
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.834
Of course, there was
a big Veterans Day Parade

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:53.934
here in New York City.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
You were there?

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:02.434
It included 25 floats,
20,000 marchers,

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.267
and one guy who was still
finishing the marathon.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.834
[ Laughter ]
[ Southern accent ]
Alright, you can do it.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.200
Come on, buddy, go!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.234
Well, so many of you
in tonight's audience

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.000
earned some amazing medals
over your careers

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.968
and I think sometimes civilians
can feel a little left out,

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:17.367
so we decided
to make some medals

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.000
that regular people
can earn, too.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:19.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:21.033
I'll show you what I mean.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.501
For instance,
there's a medal for...

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:27.767
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.634
You know, I don't --
Yeah, I heard you.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:31.901
There's also a medal for...

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:37.267
It's like --
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:40.868
Next, there's a medal for....

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.133
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.300
Next, there's a medal for...

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:55.501
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:58.868
And, finally,
there's a medal for...

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:02.901
There you go, yeah.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.167
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:07.267
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.501
I'm trying! I'm trying!
I'm trying.

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:14.801
I'm so honored and thrilled
that our audience is filled

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.400
with men and women who served
in uniform.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.400
But look, I don't want to be
a stickler about this,

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.601
but when we say served
in uniform,

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:21.968
we're talking about people
in the military.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.667
so, I'm sorry, sir, but you're
going to have to leave.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.234
[ Laughter ]
-Wait, wait. No, no, hold on.

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.434
-No, no, no, I'm sorry, no.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:28.200
-Wait, just a second.
This is a uniform.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.467
-No, no.
-Come on, wait, wait, wait.

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.501
[ Cheering and applause ]
No, wait, wait, hold on.

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.000
No, no, hold on.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.467
Oh, no!
-I appreciate it, but --

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.534
-You can't handle the truth!
-No, come on.

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.133
-You can't handle the truth!
-I know, I know.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:39.868
Get him outta here.

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.334
Sorry about that.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:46.467
Let's get to some news.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:47.634
Everybody's talking
about this --

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.734
in his first address
to Twitter employees,

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:53.234
Elon Musk said that bankruptcy
is a possibility.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.000
Answering the question,
"What's the opposite

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.767
of a motivational speech?"
It's like --

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:58.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.767
Twitter also suspended
the launch of Twitter Blue

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:03.100
because so many users
were paying to be verified,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.300
then impersonating other people.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.701
[ Laughter ]
Seriously, it's a mess
over there.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.167
I knew the impersonations
were a problem

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.167
when Pope Francis slid
into my DMs.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.834
It was weird.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.133
And did you see this?
I read that

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:18.601
almost every major
cryptocurrency is crashing.

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.467
Right now, the only
Bitcoin winners are the people

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.467
who never wasted the time
to understand it.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.901
[ Laughter, cheering,
whistling, and applause ]

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.067
[Indistinct].

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.467
It's pretty shocking.
It turns out fake money is not

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:31.767
as valuable as you think.

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:33.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:35.033
Some news from overseas --

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:38.167
today President Biden was
at a climate summit in Egypt

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:39.801
and, during his speech,
someone interrupted him

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:41.434
with a loud sound.
Check this out.

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.367
-[ Echoing ]
As I stand here before you,

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.434
we've taken enormous strides
to achieve that.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:50.200
-[ Howling echoes ]

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.200
-But I don't stand here alone.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:56.100
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.567
-No, you're not --

00:03:58.567 --> 00:03:59.634
No, you're not alone.

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.200
It's you and a pack of coyotes.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:04.968
You can tell, for a second,
Biden was like,

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:07.067
"Please tell me you guys
are hearing this sound, too.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.534
It's not my time yet, please.
It's not my --"

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:14.801
Some entertainment news --
I saw that a biopic

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:17.167
about Snoop Dogg's life is
in the works

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:18.167
and, right now,
they're trying to figure out

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:20.234
the best name for the movie.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.767
For example, they're
considering names like --

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.767
-Ah, here we go.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.400
[ Laughter ]
-What's up, Tariq?

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.667
-Let me guess.

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:29.067
You're going to list
a bunch of fake movie titles

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.868
about Snoop Dogg, right?

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:31.901
-I mean, yeah,
that was the plan.

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:32.901
-And then, then, like

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:34.100
a little graphic'll pop up,

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.601
so everyone could see the titles
and laugh along.

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:39.400
-Right, I want to show
our audience a good time.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.467
-Yeah, I know exactly
how this'll go down.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.367
See, first, a graphic'll pop up

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:45.234
with a picture of Snoop Dogg
that says...

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.300
-Yeah.
-And then, and then, under that,

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.334
you'll list the fake titles,
like, like...

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:53.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:54.934
Or, or, or...

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.868
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.000
I'm just spitballing here.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.434
Stuff like, uh...

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.334
[ Laughter ]
And then, and then,
of course, the...

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.234
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
You know...

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.200
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:12.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
-What?!

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:13.501
-And then you'll do, you know...

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:16.400
[ Laughter ]
...or something like that.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.267
-Yeah.
-Oh, and, uh...

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.067
Followed by...

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:24.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.467
And then --

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:30.234
And then you'll probably end
on something topical,

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:32.033
like, I don't know,
instead of "John Wick,"

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.200
you'll just go with...

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:35.200
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.300
-Is that how this
is going to go?

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.934
-Yeah. You nailed it.
-Cool.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.400
It's a fun bit.
You should do it.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.067
[ Laughter ]
-Alright. We'll do it next week.

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.734
Thank you.
I'll do it next week.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:47.634
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:49.100
"Wakanda For-Reefer"?

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.701
Hey, guys, get this --
I heard that the
National Toy Hall of Fame

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:56.000
just inducted the top,
Lite-Brite,

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.033
and Masters of the Universe.

00:05:58.033 --> 00:06:00.701
Yep, they praised Lite-Brite
for introducing millions of kids

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:03.167
to the feeling of being burnt
by a scalding-hot lightbulb.

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:05.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:07.801
That's right, this year's
Toy Hall of Fame inductees

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:10.601
are the top, Lite-Brite,
and Masters of the Universe.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:12.334
And this is very interesting --
they also announced a list

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:14.000
of the worst toys.
-Really?!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.100
-Yeah.
Check out some of these.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:15.968
First up, there's...

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:20.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:21.300
Next up, there's...

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:25.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
Sad.

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:26.133
Next, there's...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.400
[ Laughter and ewws ]

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.534
-Ugh! Wow!
[ Rimshot ]

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:35.601
-I can't believe we showed that
on television.

00:06:35.601 --> 00:06:37.601
-Oh, my God!
Pre-Dropped?

00:06:37.601 --> 00:06:39.601
-Oh, my gosh.
-Oh, my God!

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:41.234
And, finally,
the worst toy of all...

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:45.400
[ Laughter, oohs, and applause ]

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.868
[ Cheering ]
Tickles you back. Weird.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.734
Finally, this is exciting --
tomorrow,

00:06:51.734 --> 00:06:54.701
the Rockefeller Center
Christmas Tree is going up.

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:57.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:59.667
It kicks off that special
two months in New York City

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:01.100
when even Navy SEALs are like,

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.133
"Let's get the hell outta here."

